From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor <victor@local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tp: 0018 attention shard kill switches for the dist path

The same-host TP path has had SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_KDA / SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_MLA
since kimi_k3_tp.cpp:350. The DISTRIBUTED path had neither: it took
ShardPolicy::ExpertsAndAttn from a struct default in kimi_k3_dist_rank.h and
nothing ever assigned it, so attention sharding was the one major code path in
the multi-Spark engine that could not be A/B'd against itself on one binary.
Every other knob in the engine is same-binary switchable; this one was not, and
it is the one that governs 93 layers of attention math.

This adds the two switches to the dist path under the SAME NAMES, so a flag
learned on one path means the same thing on the other. Unset means ON, so the
default resolves to ExpertsAndAttn -- byte-for-byte the previous behavior. The
resolved policy is printed once per rank at load so a run's logs record what it
actually ran rather than what the launcher intended.

Used to establish, on the live 3-Spark fleet, that MLA head sharding is
numerically correct: with SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_MLA=0 the per-layer residual
stream matches the sharded run to relL2 8.2e-09 at the first MLA layer (layer
3) -- i.e. pure float reassociation from summing 96 heads as 3x32 partials
instead of all at once, which is exactly what a correct shard+all-reduce should
cost. Downstream layers diverge chaotically from that 1e-8 seed (2e-4 by layer
7, 5e-2 by layer 13), which is amplification, not error.

NOTE ON MEMORY, since this bit me: SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_KDA=0 does NOT fit on a
121 GB GB10. Replicating the 69 KDA layers' attention at full width OOMs during
load at blk.84.attn_k.weight, and turning both switches off OOMs at
blk.82.attn_output.weight. Only the MLA switch is usable as a correctness A/B on
this hardware; the KDA one needs a bigger box.

DEPLOYMENT WARNING, unrelated to this patch but discovered while testing it:
almost all engine code, including the whole dist forward, compiles into
libsparkinfer_runtime.so, NOT into the kimi_k3_dist_generate executable, and
dist/ is on LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Copying only the executable to the worker nodes
ships a new launcher against the OLD runtime and fails SILENTLY -- no version
check, no error, it just runs the previous code. Deploy both, and verify with
  strings dist/libsparkinfer_runtime.so | grep <a string from your change>
---
 runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_dist_rank.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_dist_rank.cpp b/runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_dist_rank.cpp
--- a/runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_dist_rank.cpp
+++ b/runtime/src/models/kimi_k3_dist_rank.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include "sparkinfer/models/kimi_k3_gguf_config.h"

 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <string>

 namespace sparkinfer {
@@ -93,7 +94,27 @@ bool kimi_k3_dist_rank_load(const std::string& gguf_first_shard,
         return false;
     }

-    out->weights.policy = opt.policy;
+    // Attention-sharding kill switches, same flag names as the same-host TP path
+    // (kimi_k3_tp.cpp). The dist path hardcoded ExpertsAndAttn with no override,
+    // which left attention sharding the one major path that could not be A/B'd
+    // against itself on one binary. Unset => on => ExpertsAndAttn, i.e. no change.
+    {
+        auto shard_on = [](const char* n) {
+            const char* e = std::getenv(n);
+            return !(e && e[0] == '0');
+        };
+        const bool k = shard_on("SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_KDA") && spec.world_size > 1;
+        const bool m = shard_on("SPARKINFER_K3_SHARD_MLA") && spec.world_size > 1;
+        const KimiK3Weights::ShardPolicy p =
+            (k && m) ? KimiK3Weights::ShardPolicy::ExpertsAndAttn :
+            k        ? KimiK3Weights::ShardPolicy::ExpertsAndKda  :
+            m        ? KimiK3Weights::ShardPolicy::ExpertsAndMla  :
+                       KimiK3Weights::ShardPolicy::ExpertsOnly;
+        std::fprintf(stderr, "[k3-dist] rank%d shard policy=%d (shard_kda=%d shard_mla=%d)\n",
+                     spec.rank, (int)p, (int)k, (int)m);
+        out->weights.policy = p;
+    }
     out->weights.shard = out->plan.dims;
     out->weights.shard.tp_size = spec.world_size;
     out->weights.shard.rank = spec.rank;
--
2.43.0
